113
00:19:22.500 --> 00:19:42.450
Yu Cheng: The first question is very simple, like, what are you trying to explain? Are you trying to understand the whole model, or are you… or just one specific prediction? If you care about the whole model, for example, which features matter overall, then use the global methods on the left hand.

114
00:19:42.910 --> 00:19:47.259
Yu Cheng: For a tree-based model, like, actually boast or random forests.

115
00:19:47.450 --> 00:19:55.099
Yu Cheng: tree sharp is actually the best choice. For general models, we can use methods like PDP or ALE.

116
00:19:55.640 --> 00:20:01.720
Yu Cheng: And if the features are highly correlated, we can choose the ALE instead of the PDP.

117
00:20:01.840 --> 00:20:17.700
Yu Cheng: On the other hand, if you want to explain one specific prediction, then we move to local methods. For neural networks, we often use integrity gradients. For general black box model, we use LIME or SHOP.

118
00:20:18.380 --> 00:20:27.550
Yu Cheng: And then it depends on the question, like, do you want to ask, why did this happen? You want to know the reason, or you want to ask

